risk:
It reads journals the perch did not write (a run session in eidolon's own folder), so security_review stays true. The reviewer confirms:
(1) every journal string, the no-drawing line and the labels included, goes through clean and is drawn as text, as W2b-2's view does;
(2) the only read is sessions/<id>/log, with an id that passed the id rule; the key fails ridOk, so no runs/ path and no perch verb is built; there is no hubPost;
(3) readonly cannot be turned off from a journal: it is a constant in ChatRunView.
The reads are whole logs, so they are rationed by mtime. A run started outside the perch is under neither the one-browser cap nor the mock-only rule (R1a). That is GW's concern (named in PR's notes), not this view's.
